    "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 13-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Optimize a 13-layer planar multilayer stack on Al substrate with material sequence: Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr (13 finite layers total). Initialize thicknesses at [67.27, 211.32, 141.72, 171.96, 203.32, 81.53, 48.56, 89.73, 121.81, 105.50, 134.05, 107.60, 101.25] nm with ±8% random perturbations. Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with step-size multiplier reduced to 0.5x. Thickness bounds: [30, 300] nm for all layers. Spectral objectives: maximize absorptance in 400-700 nm, maximize reflectance in 700-2000 nm. Normal incidence, unpolarized light. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
